STEP 2: Calculate pi (CPU work)
-------------------------------
vi job-pi.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: pi
spec:
  ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 300
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
      - name: pi
        image: perl:5.40
        command: ["perl", "-Mbignum=bpi", "-wle", "print bpi(1000)"]

k apply -f job-pi.yaml
k wait --for=condition=complete job/pi --timeout=120s
k logs job/pi | cut -c1-80

After 5 minutes the Job deletes itself (ttlSecondsAfterFinished).


STEP 3: Parallel Job with fixed completions
-------------------------------------------
vi job-parallel.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: batch
spec:
  completions: 6
  parallelism: 2
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
      - name: worker
        image: busybox:1.36
        command: ["sh", "-c", "echo processing on $(hostname); sleep 8"]

Terminal 2: k get pods -l job-name=batch -w
k apply -f job-parallel.yaml

Two pods at a time, six total. Change parallelism to 3 in the file,
delete the Job, and run it again. Compare the total time:
  k get job batch -o jsonpath='{.status.startTime} -> {.status.completionTime}{"\n"}'


STEP 4: Indexed Job (process shards)
------------------------------------
vi job-indexed.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: shards
spec:
  completions: 4
  parallelism: 4
  completionMode: Indexed
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
      - name: w
        image: busybox:1.36
        command: ["sh", "-c", "echo processing shard $JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX of 4"]

k apply -f job-indexed.yaml
k wait --for=condition=complete job/shards
for p in $(k get pods -l job-name=shards -o name); do k logs $p; done


STEP 5: Failures, retries, backoffLimit
---------------------------------------
vi job-fail.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: flaky
spec:
  backoffLimit: 3
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
      - name: c
        image: busybox:1.36
        command: ["sh", "-c", "echo trying; exit 1"]

k apply -f job-fail.yaml
k get pods -l job-name=flaky -w        # new pod per attempt, growing delay
k describe job flaky | tail -8           # BackoffLimitExceeded
k get job flaky -o jsonpath='{.status.conditions[*].reason}{"\n"}'

Change restartPolicy to OnFailure, delete and re-apply. Now there is
ONE pod whose RESTARTS count grows. Which is easier to debug?


