STEP 8: CronJob
---------------
vi cron-date.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: ticker
spec:
  schedule: "*/1 * * * *"
  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid
  successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3
  failedJobsHistoryLimit: 1
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          restartPolicy: OnFailure
          containers:
          - name: tick
            image: busybox:1.36
            command: ["sh", "-c", "date; echo tick"]

k apply -f cron-date.yaml
k get cronjob ticker
k get jobs -w             # a new Job every minute; only 3 kept

Trigger one now without waiting:
  k create job ticker-manual --from=cronjob/ticker
  k logs job/ticker-manual

Pause it:
  k patch cronjob ticker -p '{"spec":{"suspend":true}}'


STEP 9: concurrencyPolicy in action
-----------------------------------
Make each run take 90 s (longer than the 1-minute schedule):
  k patch cronjob ticker --type=json -p '[{"op":"replace","path":"/spec/jobTemplate/spec/template/spec/containers/0/command","value":["sh","-c","date; sleep 90"]},{"op":"replace","path":"/spec/suspend","value":false}]'
Watch for 4 minutes: k get jobs -w
With Forbid, runs are skipped while one is active. Change to Allow and
then Replace, and note the difference in Part C.


STEP 10: A realistic backup CronJob (Postgres dump to a PVC)
------------------------------------------------------------
Recreate the pg StatefulSet from Day 26 (sts-postgres.yaml + secret),
then:

vi cron-pgdump.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: backups
spec:
  accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi
---
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: pg-backup
spec:
  schedule: "*/2 * * * *"
  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      backoffLimit: 2
      template:
        spec:
          restartPolicy: OnFailure
          containers:
          - name: dump
            image: postgres:16
            env:
            - name: PGPASSWORD
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                  name: pg
                  key: POSTGRES_PASSWORD
            command: ["sh", "-c", "pg_dump -h pg-0.pg -U postgres postgres > /backups/dump-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).sql && ls -l /backups"]
            volumeMounts:
            - name: b
              mountPath: /backups
          volumes:
          - name: b
            persistentVolumeClaim:
              claimName: backups

k apply -f cron-pgdump.yaml
Wait 2-4 minutes, then:
  k logs job/$(k get jobs -o name | grep pg-backup | tail -1 | cut -d/ -f2)

(Note: the backups PVC is RWO and local-path is per-node, so all
backup pods will be scheduled onto the node holding the volume.)


